multer is a node js middleware for handling multipart/form-data (is a HTTP media type used to send complex data - such as text and files in a single request) which is used for uploading files. 

HTTP stands for HyperText Transfer Protocol. It is the foundation of data communication for the World Wide Web. It acts as a set of rules (or language) that allows your web browser to talk to a web server in order to load websites.

whenever a server receives a HTTP request - middleware functions intercept it - they have access to three arguments (req, res, next())

req: The Request object containing details about the client's incoming data.
res: The Response object used to send back data or HTML headers.
next(): A callback function that, when executed, passes control to the next middleware in line

Multer adds a body object and a file or files object to the request object.
The body object contains the values of the text fields of the form, the file or files object contains the files uploaded via the form.

The enctype attribute in HTML specifies how form data is encoded before being sent to a server

The HTML attribute enctype="multipart/form-data" is required whenever a web form contains a file upload input (<input type="file">). It instructs the browser to package the form data into distinct, separate segments so that complex binary files (like images, audio, or PDFs) can be successfully transmitted to the server along with normal text inputs

